course: dictionary
lesson: 5648
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «A Station Road boy shoved Maddie so hard she fell on the kerb and split her lip.» Here lip is the soft part around your mouth, because Maddie fell and hurt herself.
explain: Now read «Goats nibble paper labels and test things with their lips.» Goats use their lips to feel and test things, so lips means the soft parts of the mouth again. Ask yourself: what word would fit in its place? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Lip can also mean the edge of something. The lip of a jug, a cup or a cliff is its rim or edge. Informally, lip means rude talk, as in «don't give me any lip». The clues around the word always show you which meaning to choose.
fact: Lip is a noun. Its plural is lips.
fact: Your lips are the two soft edges around your mouth. They help you eat, speak and make sounds like «p», «b» and «m».
fact: The lip of a jug, cup or cliff is its edge or rim.
fact: Informally, «lip» means rude talk, as in «don't give me any lip».
fact: Phrases with lip: bite your lip (holding back words), my lips are sealed (I will keep a secret), stiff upper lip (staying calm and brave).
exercise: «A Station Road boy shoved Maddie so hard she fell on the kerb and split her lip.» What does lip mean here? | The edge of a jug | Rude talk | *The soft part around her mouth | The top of a cliff
exercise: The lip of the cup was chipped. What does lip mean here? | Lips that are dry and cracked | *The rim or edge of the cup | Rude talk | The soft part around a mouth
exercise: Mum says, «Don't give me any lip!» What does lip mean here? | The soft edge of the mouth | *Rude talk | A kind word | Something to drink from
test:
«Your dog is fast asleep, but its lips twitch and it gives tiny muffled woofs.» What does lips mean here? | The edge of a bowl | Rude talk | *The soft parts around its mouth | The rim of a cliff
Which sound do your lips help you make? | *«p» | «t» | «k» | «s»
exam: «A dog yawns, licks its lips and turns its head away before it bites.» What does this behaviour usually show? | A wish to play | *A warning | Hunger for dinner | Sleepiness only
